{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A column is any set of vertices: empty columns and repeated columns are kept, and a graph’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop is the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. (NetworkX’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"loop a zero column; Godsil–Royle’s entry 2 is not a bit. A zero column would forget the loop.)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the directed form; ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation of the same hypergraphs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Storage."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Both orientations are stored, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" stores its rows: n rows of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the row and column popcounts cached. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the matrix is for dense or small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidence","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidence belongs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. (","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s equality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/Se","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SE","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/SH","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"IncidenceMatrix","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix.swift#L28","fileName":"IncidenceMatrix.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init()","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4158r","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4kjv4","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/in